   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the exact value of \\( \\int_{0}^{1} x^{2} e^{x} \\, dx \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         -2,
         "ExponentialE"
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x^{2} \\) and \\( dv = e^{x} \\, dx \\), so \\( du = 2 x \\, dx \\) and \\( v = e^{x} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Exp",
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[x^{2} e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{1} - \\int_{0}^{1} 2 x e^{x} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( e \\).",
         "mathjson": "ExponentialE"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral \\( \\int_{0}^{1} 2 x e^{x} \\, dx \\) needs integration by parts once more, with the polynomial factor as the new u; it equals \\( 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( e - \\left(2\\right) = -2 + e \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            -2,
            "ExponentialE"
         ]
      }
   ],
